# T28 manual QA log — RSR-01c Playwright browser worker + local web (D13-minimal)

## 1. Sandbox-posture probe (scratch/t28-browser/probe-sandbox*.mjs)

- Playwright 1.58.2 (Node, /home/srcds/node_modules — the existing product-E2E install;
  browsers at ~/.cache/ms-playwright: chromium-1208 = Chrome for Testing 145.0.7632.6,
  chromium-1234, firefox-1509). Python playwright NOT installed — worker is a Node
  subprocess driven by the Python adapter over line-JSON stdio.
- CRITICAL: Playwright's DEFAULT chromium launch injects `--no-sandbox`
  (chromiumSandbox defaults to false). Verified by /proc cmdline scan: default launch
  → renderer carries `--no-sandbox`, Seccomp=0 (kernel seccomp OFF).
- Launch used by the worker: `{ headless: true, chromiumSandbox: true, channel: "chromium" }`
  (full version-matched Chromium binary, not the headless-shell):
  no `--no-sandbox` anywhere in the process tree; renderer processes show
  NoNewPrivs=1 + Seccomp=2. Chromium rewrites child argv (`--type` consumed), so the
  kernel-proof discriminator is Seccomp=2 — present ONLY in sandboxed renderers.
- `chrome://sandbox` navigation fails headless (ERR_INVALID_URL) — /proc-based probe
  is the honest alternative and is what startup_check implements.

