## 3. pytest integration suite (tests/unit/test_browser_worker.py)

13 passed in ~16s against the real worker + tests/fixtures/web loopback server:
startup posture proof; private targets (10/8, 192.168/16, 169.254/16 metadata,
unallowed loopback, [::1]) refused pre-connect with denial log; /private-links page
(allowed origin) whose JS probes 10.0.0.1 + 169.254.169.254 + 192.168.0.10 → every
probe "blocked", denial log carries all three (phase=route); JS-render fixture:
static httpx fetch sees only "js-stub-loading" (marker composed at runtime from
fragments so it cannot appear in static bytes) while the worker materializes
js-rendered-marker-DYNAMIC-7834; disposable contexts (session A localStorage never
reaches session B); downloads land in quarantine with exact bytes and the oversized
one is refused (download_limit_exceeded, file deleted); /slow?delay_ms=8000 with a
1000ms nav budget → typed navigation_timeout; redirect chain resolves to final URL;
403 page records http_status; robots.txt + disallowed private page readable as data;
injection page observed strictly as data; executor journey (fetch fails → gate
authorizes → browser.open/observe → finish) with evidence rows.

Executor gate units (tests/unit/test_research_executor.py): 11 passed —
unauthorized browser.open denied + audited (browser_automation_not_authorized);
allowed via approved workflow; allowed after failed static fetch of the SAME url.

